# Heartbeats - chassis template

**This file is the chassis template.** It is NOT read by the dispatcher. At install-time, `bootstrap.sh` copies this template to `${CUSTOMER_HOME}/HEARTBEATS.md`. The installer edits the rendered file at `${CUSTOMER_HOME}/HEARTBEATS.md`, never this template.

Why: per `docs/architectural-anti-patterns.md` #17, customizations live OUTSIDE `chassis/`. The dispatcher reads `${CUSTOMER_HOME}/HEARTBEATS.md`; this template ships from chassis with the schema docs only.

---

## Path conventions

After #6 split CUSTOMER_HOME from CHASSIS_HOME, picking the right env var for `gather` and `prompt` paths matters:

| Scenario | Use this | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Invoking a chassis-shipped script | `${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/scripts/...` | `gather: ${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/scripts/gather-local-health.sh` |
| Invoking a chassis-shipped prompt | `${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/scheduled-tasks/...` | `prompt: ${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/scheduled-tasks/example-prompt.md` |
| Invoking your own gather (customer-side) | `${CUSTOMER_HOME}/scheduled-tasks/...` | `gather: ${CUSTOMER_HOME}/scheduled-tasks/gather-morning-briefing.sh` |
| Invoking your own prompt (customer-side) | `${CUSTOMER_HOME}/scheduled-tasks/prompts/...` | `prompt: ${CUSTOMER_HOME}/scheduled-tasks/prompts/morning-briefing.md` |

Rule of thumb: if the script or prompt ships with the chassis (lives under `${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/`), use CHASSIS_HOME. If you wrote it for this install (lives under `${CUSTOMER_HOME}/`), use CUSTOMER_HOME. Mixing them up resolves to the wrong tree post-migration - see Toby case study in #6.

### Containerized installs: the first two rows do not apply (#151)

The rows above describe a HOST-side install, where `CHASSIS_HOME` is the chassis git tree. Inside the container `CHASSIS_HOME` is the CUSTOMER root (`/app/customer`) and the chassis tree is somewhere else entirely - `/app/chassis` on a baked install, `/app/customer/chassis/chassis` when a chassis clone is mounted at `$CUSTOMER_HOME/chassis`. `${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/scripts/...` names neither.

Two separate failures follow, and both are silent:

- **gather**: the line is `eval`ed with cwd `$CUSTOMER_HOME`, so the variable expands - to a path that does not exist. The heartbeat logs `gather script failed` every tick.
- **prompt**: prompt paths are NOT variable-expanded. The dispatcher joins the raw string onto `$CHASSIS_HOME`, so a `${CHASSIS_HOME}/...` prompt becomes the literal `/app/customer/${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/...` and the heartbeat dies with `prompt_missing` the first time it fires.

For chassis-shipped scripts and prompts on a containerized install, address them through the boot-time chassis-root symlink, relative to `$CUSTOMER_HOME`:

```yaml
gather: state/chassis-root/scripts/gather-memory-canary.sh
prompt: state/chassis-root/scheduled-tasks/memory-canary-prompt.md
```

`state/chassis-root` is materialized by `resolve-chassis-root.sh` at every container boot and always points at the tree the dispatcher is actually running, on both the baked and the mounted-clone layout. The gather resolves because the dispatcher runs gathers with cwd `$CUSTOMER_HOME`; the prompt resolves through the same `$CHASSIS_HOME`/`$CUSTOMER_HOME` join, both of which are `/app/customer` in the container.

A host-side install that runs the dispatcher directly from launchd never executes the resolving entrypoint, so it has no `state/chassis-root`. There, keep the literal chassis tree path: `${CHASSIS_HOME}/chassis/scripts/...` for the gather, and a `$CHASSIS_HOME`-relative path with no variable in it for the prompt (`chassis/scheduled-tasks/...`).

---

Declarative work queue for the chassis heartbeat dispatcher (`chassis/scheduled-tasks/heartbeat-dispatcher.sh`). Each `##` section defines a heartbeat: when to check, how to gather data, when to fire Claude.

> **Per LESSONS_FROM_V1.md #11:** scaffolding a heartbeat (script + prompt + state file) without registering it here means the dispatcher never invokes it. Silent dormancy. **Register every new heartbeat in this file in the same PR as the supporting scripts.**
>
> **Per #20:** the gather script is the right place for expensive checks to no-op cheaply. Every dispatcher tick (~96/day) is fine IF the gather short-circuits on trivial conditions before any paid API call.
>
> **Per #14:** validate this file's YAML blocks parse cleanly before commit. A malformed YAML block silently disables the heartbeat without erroring.

